# NGINX.CONF.EXAMPLE
#
# PHASE: 1
#
# NOTE ON FILENAME: nginx doesn't care about case, but the actual deployed
# file on the VPS should be placed as lowercase per standard convention:
#   /etc/nginx/sites-available/ddos-shield
# This .EXAMPLE file is the source of truth kept in the repo (ALL CAPS,
# per project convention); copy its contents to a lowercase file on the
# server itself.
#
# WHAT GOES HERE (Phase 1):
#   - limit_req_zone for per-IP rate limiting
#   - limit_conn_zone for connection caps (Slowloris defense)
#   - proxy_pass to gunicorn (127.0.0.1:8080 or a unix socket)
#   - reasonable client_body_timeout / client_header_timeout
#   - HTTPS server block (Certbot-managed certs)
#
# NOT YET IMPLEMENTED -- placeholder only.
